  "ito2021_relationship": "Same lab (Sellers; T. Ito is an author of both), same three cell lines (probably the same Cas9-expressing derivatives), different library. Ito 2021 used the spCas9-saCas9 orthologous system; Li 2022 re-uses exactly those published Ito screens as its 10th ('spCas9-saCas9') architecture. Our labels come from the new VCR1-WCR3 dual-spCas9 library: 681 of 3,674 Li spCas9 guide sequences (19%) also occur as spCas9 guides in the Ito library (checked from figshare Raw_Data Minilib_Annotation.rds vs SpSa_Annotation.rds); saCas9 guides are all different. So this is partly-shared-reagent, same-lab replication, not fully independent.",
  "chou2025_note": "Hart lab, enCas12a in4mer, MelJuso: independent lab and reagents, same line. 104 overlapping pairs: chou ZdLFC for our labels 0.886 (5 pos); our z for chou labels 0.790 (15 pos).",
